  "name": "self-model-theory",
  "title": "Self-Model Theory of Subjectivity",
  "role": "model",
  "summary": "Thomas Metzinger's self-model theory of subjectivity: no such things as selves exist. What appears as a self is the content of a transparent phenomenal self-model, a model the brain cannot recognize as a model, and the first-person perspective is a model of the system directed at the world. Phenomenal experience itself stays real, as representational content of the brain.",
